# GitHub shows "Cite this repository" from this file. Whoever uses the whistle model should also cite Park et al. (references).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. If you use its whistle model, please also cite Park et al. (2026), listed under references."
title: "Falsetto: short text messages hidden in synthetic false killer whale whistles"
type: software
abstract: >-
  A biomimetic underwater messaging system, built as an independent student course project. A sender turns text into
  whistles meant to pass for false killer whales: each whistle carries 6 bits as one of 16 shapes from a generative
  model at one of 4 key-chosen pitches, placed at real whistle times among cover whistles. A receiver holding the key
  recovers the exact text. The whistle model follows the VAE-GMM method of Park et al. (IEEE Access, 2026), trained on
  NOAA DCLDE 2022 recordings with a newly designed whistle detector; the project is not affiliated with that paper's
  authors. Tested in simulation with real ocean noise only.
authors:
  - name: "anonymus-k-dot"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.10.0
date-released: 2026-11-22
repository-code: "https://github.com/anonymus-k-dot/cetacean_whistle_reproduction"
keywords:
  - biomimetic underwater communication
  - covert communication
  - bioacoustics
  - cetacean whistles
  - variational autoencoder
  - gaussian mixture model
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A Generative Model for Cetacean Whistles Using Variational Autoencoder and Mixture of Gaussians"
    authors:
